From 14472839cc21858694db607571ba5cc24b52587e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stripe opposite-peer payloads over four reciprocal mesh paths

Upstream-base: 236ddff04a5f5064084b46464800b70b34ec7d8c plus deployment patches 0001-0007.

Rationale: retain two direct neighbor paths and use four paths for the opposite peer. Mixed-width mesh geometry uses four flag slots and waits only on active paths. B12X_ROCE_MESH_ROTATE optionally rotates HCA and traffic-class posting order without changing the byte split or introducing a completion barrier. ABI 8 rejects incompatible geometry and rotation settings.

Quality: payload byte offsets and fixed-rank GPU arithmetic are unchanged. The GPU completion predicate includes all four opposite-path flags and two neighbor flags; inactive neighbor slots are excluded. Malformed path counts and duplicate neighbor HCAs fail closed.

Tests: 26,000 real-proxy simulated collectives under ASan/UBSan, fixed and rotating posts, delayed DMA, uneven small payloads, sequence wrap, geometry mismatch and stop/error tests. Simulator verifies posting order and every delivered byte. Hardware qualification remains required.

Upstream-status: local experiment; not submitted.
